From 55d2da7ed2672b2cacb3e4d74426b1b4c7515ae7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Reimann <magnus.reimann@mailbox.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:57:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH hurd 0/5] Races in libports, libfshelp, libpager and pflocal seen on SMP

Hello,

These are races in the Hurd libraries that showed up when running
Debian GNU/Hurd amd64 with gnumach's processors all in the default
processor set (see the gnumach series sent to bug-hurd), under a
parallel build/sort/tar/fork stress test on 2 vCPUs:

1-2. libports: two threads can both see a port become unreferenced and
     both deallocate it; and ports_lookup_payload can take a reference
     on a port_info that is being freed.
3.   libfshelp: releasing a record lock freed it right after waking up
     the threads blocked on it in F_SETLKW, which then touched freed
     memory (found with a quarantining malloc in ext2fs, during flock on
     /var/lib/wtmpdb/wtmp.db).
4.   libpager: _pager_lock_object and pager_change_attributes used the
     control port without the interlock while memory_object_terminate
     could destroy it (gnumach: "task ext2fs looked up a bogus port ...
     for 2095").
5.   pflocal: when a bound socket's last user port and its address port
     went away together (processes dying at boot or shutdown),
     sock_deref and addr_unbind both unbound the socket, and pflocal
     aborted on assert_backtrace (!err) in sock_deref, taking down every
     Unix socket of the system.  Seen in 3 of 4 boots on 2 vCPUs; none
     in 6 boots with the fix.

Testing: the deployed Debian hurd 0.9.git20250801 was rebuilt in a
Hurd VM with these changes (for libports adapted to that version, where
the hash table holds no reference: the final transition is (0, 0)),
and ext2fs.static was relinked with them.  With them, the glibc fix
sent to libc-alpha and the netdde/libddekit timer fix, the stress test
passes 6 times out of 6; before, the root ext2fs corrupted its heap or
hung in most runs.  Patches 3 to 5 were compiled in that tree as they
are here; 1 and 2 only in the adapted form.

This work was done together with Claude (an AI model by Anthropic),
hence the Co-Authored-By trailers.

Magnus Reimann (5):
  libports: drop the last reference with the hash table lock held
  libports: do not free port_info under the feet of payload lookups
  libfshelp: do not free a record lock under the feet of its waiters
  libpager: do not use the control port while the object may terminate
  pflocal: unbind a socket with its address locked

 libfshelp/rlock-drop-peropen.c | 17 ++++---
 libfshelp/rlock-tweak.c        | 51 ++++++++++++---------
 libfshelp/rlock.h              |  4 ++
 libpager/lock-object.c         |  4 ++
 libpager/pager-attr.c          | 13 ++++--
 libports/complete-deallocate.c | 19 ++++----
 libports/port-deref-deferred.c | 27 +++++++++--
 libports/port-deref-deferred.h |  3 ++
 libports/port-deref-weak.c     | 11 ++++-
 libports/port-deref.c          | 20 ++++++--
 libports/ports.h               |  8 +++-
 libshouldbeinlibc/refcount.h   | 83 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 pflocal/sock.c                 | 76 ++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 pflocal/sock.h                 | 14 ++++--
 14 files changed, 261 insertions(+), 89 deletions(-)

